config:
schema_version: 1
identity:
  model: gru
  version: v021
  parent: gru_v017
  status: finished
description: dozken's reset2k architecture, trained on our own data. 2x192 GRU with
  a 64-unit GELU+LayerNorm input projection over concat[normalised, first differences]
  (224), a skip from that projection into a 256-unit MLP head, and periodic state
  reset every 2,000 rows. 435,714 params, matching the public 0.6569 model structurally
  but with none of its weights.
hypothesis: Our base is 0.0054 behind his at the base (v011 0.6515 vs his 0.6569)
  while we gained MORE from distillation than he did (+0.0027 vs +0.0019), so the
  deficit is entirely in the base architecture, not in the distillation process. His
  base is 435k params at 92-100% of the latency budget; ours is 192k at 43-52%. If
  capacity and these three structural additions (input projection, projection-to-readout
  skip, MLP head) are the cause, this closes the gap using only our own data.
change_vs_parent: 'Architecture, plus chunk_len 2000 -> 1000 so it is required. StatefulBatchStream
  refuses state_reset <= chunk_len: a reset landing on every chunk boundary would
  discard all carried state and leave the model with no memory beyond one chunk. His
  reset period is 2,000, so chunk_len must be smaller; 1,000 divides 20,000 and puts
  the reset every 2 chunks, keeping one chunk of carry. It is also the chunk size
  his own notes cite. Otherwise: hidden 96->192, input_proj 0->64, linear head ->
  LayerNorm + 192-unit GELU MLP over concat[h2, projection], first_differences []->all
  112 columns, normalisation none->robust_zscore clip_sigma 10, state_reset 4000->2000.
  Loss, optimiser and data unchanged.'
